From: =?UTF-8?q?Eduardo=20Garc=C3=ADa-M=C3=A1dico=20Portabella?=
 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 00:48:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7325-nothing-spacewar: S5KJN1 link
 frequency is 700 MHz

The S5KJN1 driver only lists a 700 MHz link frequency (the 19.2 MHz MCLK
settings keep the same output PLL as the 24 MHz ones), while the ultra
wide camera endpoint asked for 600 MHz: the sensor failed to probe with
"no matching link frequencies found", and CAMSS, waiting for every
sensor in its graph, never registered the front camera either.

Use 700 MHz, as in the spacewar-next tree.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts
index f87710062..ad3907919 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts
@@ -973,7 +973,7 @@ port {
 			camera_s5kjn1_ep: endpoint {
 				data-lanes = <1 2 3 4>;
 				bus-type = <MEDIA_BUS_TYPE_CSI2_DPHY>;
-				link-frequencies = /bits/ 64 <600000000>;
+				link-frequencies = /bits/ 64 <700000000>;
 				remote-endpoint = <&csiphy2_ep>;
 			};
 		};
-- 
